<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Scrolling on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/scrolling/</link><description>Recent content in Scrolling on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 19 Mar 2013 10:13:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/scrolling/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Arduino LCD Message Scroller working</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-message-scroller-working/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 Mar 2013 10:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-lcd-message-scroller-working/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Got my Arduino LCD message scroller working last night, will post a video later when I do an end to end test with my Twitter mentions.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/g2Ql86wt8dI/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/g2Ql86wt8dI?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Here is the code (also at GitHub &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/arduino.git&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Auto&amp;nbsp;scroll&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;message&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;LCD&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;receive&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;messages&amp;nbsp;via&amp;nbsp;Serial&amp;nbsp;port.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;(c)&amp;nbsp;2013&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;Version&amp;nbsp;1.02&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;//&amp;nbsp;include&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;library&amp;nbsp;code:&lt;/span&gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt;.h&amp;gt;&#10;#include&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;string.h&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the library with the numbers of the interface pins&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// below for SainSmart LCD Shield&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;LiquidCrystal&lt;/span&gt; lcd(8, 9, 4, 5, 6, 7);&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>